# Quality Gates

No task is "Done" without documented automated verification.

**Required gate:**

```bash
pnpm verify
```

Equivalent to `pnpm build && pnpm test && pnpm lint && pnpm format:check` (that order). Still **one** required gate — no Quick/Full/Build tiers.

`pnpm test` runs Vitest with coverage (`vitest run --coverage`). Thresholds and include/exclude rules: [`.specs/codebase/TESTING.md`](../../.specs/codebase/TESTING.md) § Coverage.

To run and report: agent `verifier-quality-gates` or inline after implementation.

## Commit hook scope (gate-before-commit)

The `gate-before-commit.mjs` hook may allow a `git commit` when no tracked code path changed (for example `tests/`-only edits). The project gate above is still required before marking work **Done**.

Tracked-path SoT: `CODE_PATH_RE` in [`.cursor/hooks/lib/paths.mjs`](../hooks/lib/paths.mjs) — behavior map in [`.cursor/hooks/README.md`](../hooks/README.md). Do not restate the path list here.

When the user may commit: [commit-policy.mdc](commit-policy.mdc).
